==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|mawk}}, {{m|enm|mauk}}, a contraction of {{m|enm|mathek}}, from {{etyl|non|en}} {{m|non|maðkr||maggot}}, a diminutive of a base from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*maþô||worm}} (Old English ''[[maþa]]''), from Indo-European ''*math-, moth-'' used in reference to insects and vermin. Cognate with Danish ''[[madike]]'', Swedish ''[[mask]]'', archaic English ''[[maddock]]'' (modern ''[[maggot]]'').

